Package: pull-vids
Version: 0.2.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ffmpeg
Suggests: python3-pip
Maintainer: pull-vids contributors <https://github.com/vib795/pull-vids>
Homepage: https://github.com/vib795/pull-vids
Description: Universal video downloader CLI supporting 1000+ websites
 A free, open-source CLI tool for downloading videos and audio from 1000+
 websites. Inspired by tools like Downie and PullTube, but completely free!
 .
 Supported platforms: YouTube, Vimeo, Twitter/X, TikTok, Instagram, Facebook,
 Twitch, Reddit, Dailymotion, and 1000+ more!
 .
 Features:
  - Download videos from 1000+ websites
  - Various quality options (360p to 4K)
  - Audio-only extraction (MP3, M4A, etc.)
  - Playlist and channel support
  - Beautiful real-time progress bars
  - Fast startup (< 1ms)
 .
 Note: Requires yt-dlp to be installed (pip install yt-dlp)
